WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.335
Lesson 12.6.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.450
Books, records and succession.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.574
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:06.574 --> 00:00:09.002
to keep books a stranger could follow, and make

00:00:09.002 --> 00:00:11.935
sure your family could recover everything if you couldn't.

00:00:13.235 --> 00:00:14.525
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.525 --> 00:00:16.210
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.925
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.925 --> 00:00:20.450
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.612
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.912 --> 00:00:27.258
Books (update weekly from your journal, Module 8):

00:00:27.258 --> 00:00:30.866
Succession: self-custody means that if you're gone and

00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:33.397
nobody can sign, the money is gone

00:00:33.397 --> 00:00:36.000
too. the documents are, who to contact),

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.476
stored separately from any seed or key

00:00:38.476 --> 00:00:42.159
First, every position: protocol, chain, contract, amount,

00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:44.935
entry date and price, cost basis. Next,

00:00:44.935 --> 00:00:47.293
every loan: collateral, debt, rate, HF,

00:00:47.293 --> 00:00:49.657
action levels. Then, every approval

00:00:49.657 --> 00:00:53.132
granted, and when it was revoked. Also, Income

00:00:53.132 --> 00:00:56.152
received, by source and date. On top

00:00:56.152 --> 00:00:59.472
of that, keep exportable records for tax. Rules

00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:03.447
differ by country, so use a crypto-aware tax professional.

00:01:04.747 --> 00:01:06.710
And A letter of instruction that

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.687
explains the setup (wallets, multisig, where.

00:01:09.687 --> 00:01:13.335
Plus, Multisig with a trusted co-signer or professional

00:01:13.335 --> 00:01:16.892
service, so recovery doesn't depend on one person.

00:01:16.892 --> 00:01:20.224
One more: Legal documents (will, powers of attorney)

00:01:20.224 --> 00:01:23.542
that reference the digital assets: use a lawyer.

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:26.039
And finally, Annual drill: walk a trusted

00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:29.131
person through the letter without revealing secrets.

00:01:30.432 --> 00:01:32.947
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:32.947 --> 00:01:35.880
A 2-of-3 vault: you hold two keys (home

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.986
+ safe-deposit box); a professional co-signer holds the

00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:43.146
third under an agreed recovery process.

00:01:43.146 --> 00:01:46.038
Your letter of instruction, stored with your will,

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:49.286
explains how your executor works with the co-signer.

00:01:49.286 --> 00:01:52.684
No single document contains enough to steal the funds.

00:01:53.984 --> 00:01:55.444
Here's your checklist.

00:01:55.444 --> 00:01:56.979
Do it now, for real.

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.114
First, Books current within a week.

00:01:59.114 --> 00:02:02.829
Next, Tax records exportable; professional engaged.

00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:04.843
Then, Letter of instruction written

00:02:04.843 --> 00:02:06.654
and stored apart from keys.

00:02:06.654 --> 00:02:09.219
And finally, Annual succession drill done.

00:02:10.519 --> 00:02:11.729
Question 1.

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:13.640
Why keep the letter of instruction

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.059
apart from seeds and keys?

00:02:19.479 --> 00:02:21.314
The answer: So finding the letter

00:02:21.314 --> 00:02:23.042
isn't enough to steal the funds.

00:02:24.341 --> 00:02:25.586
Question 2.

00:02:25.586 --> 00:02:28.821
What's the risk of single-key self-custody for your family?

00:02:33.241 --> 00:02:35.456
The answer: If you can't sign and no

00:02:35.456 --> 00:02:38.031
one else can, the assets are unrecoverable.

00:02:39.331 --> 00:02:40.601
Question 3.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.376
What goes in the books for each loan?

00:02:46.796 --> 00:02:49.246
The answer: Collateral, debt, rate, health

00:02:49.246 --> 00:02:50.956
factor and your action levels.

00:02:52.256 --> 00:02:53.501
Let's recap.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:56.931
Every position: protocol, chain, contract, amount,

00:02:56.931 --> 00:02:59.451
entry date and price, cost basis.

00:02:59.451 --> 00:03:03.698
Every loan: collateral, debt, rate, HF, action levels.

00:03:03.698 --> 00:03:06.718
Every approval granted, and when it was revoked.

00:03:06.718 --> 00:03:08.898
Income received, by source and date.

00:03:10.198 --> 00:03:12.713
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:12.713 --> 00:03:17.733
Next up, Lesson 12.7: Tax, regulation and compliance awareness.
